# clang-tidy's checks of the C code, warnings as errors. Left out: swappable parameters, which C's
# pointer and size pairs always are; C11's Annex K (memcpy_s, sscanf_s), which glibc doesn't have;
# integer to pointer casts, which a patcher needs to address the code; and implicit conversions to bool,
# as C's comparisons and logical operators yield an int.
Checks: >-
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  -performance-no-int-to-ptr,
  -readability-implicit-bool-conversion
WarningsAsErrors: "*"
